7              -> digit
42             -> integer
2.5            -> digit
9.5            -> float
"case"         -> keyword
"ruby"         -> word
"Ruby"         -> something else
[1, 2, 3, 4]   -> long array
nil            -> something else

(1..9) === 2.5 -> true: a Range answers === with cover?, so 2.5 is a "digit"
move `when Float` above the Range if that is not what you meant
